WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.000
The Joker is Batman's greatest villain and
one of the best bad guys in comic book history.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:10.100
He's willing to anything, no matter how psychotic,
to convince Batman that morality and order

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.220
are just a fantasy.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.260
Here are the most terrible things he's done
to make that point.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.259
Of all the atrocities he's ever committed,
the Joker is probably best known for paralyzing

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.180
Barbara Gordon.

00:00:20.529 --> 00:00:25.120
The grisly act occurs in Alan Moore and Brian
Bolland's infamous graphic novel, Batman:

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:25.840
The Killing Joke.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.359
In an effort to prove that everyone is only
one bad day away from being just like him,

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:34.641
the Joker does his best and worst to drive
the Dark Knight's most trusted ally, Commissioner

00:00:34.641 --> 00:00:38.120
Jim Gordon, to becoming a blubbering heap
of his former self.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:41.040
So how does he plan on destroying Batman's
best friend?

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.990
He simply knocks on Barbara Gordon's door,
and when the commissioner's daughter says

00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:46.400
hello, the Joker shoots her.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.640
The bullet shatters her spine, leaving her
paralyzed from the waist down, and, while

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:55.060
the Joker didn't know it at the time, putting
an end to her crime-fighting career as Batgirl.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:01:00.580
Then, adding insult to injury, the Joker takes
photos of his truly horrific violation, projecting

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.870
them onto screens and forcing the Commissioner
to look at them while he puts him through

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.520
a carnival funhouse that's been twisted into
a psychological torture chamber.

00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.140
The story is both hugely controversial and
genuinely disturbing, and is still considered

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.740
to be the worst thing he's ever done over
30 years after it was first published.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.140
In the aftermath of The Killing Joke, it's
easy to think that the Gordon family had suffered

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:20.640
enough.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.420
In December of 1999, however, the Joker decided
to take another brutal shot at his least-favorite

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:26.820
law enforcing family.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.300
This time, the target was Sarah Essen-Gordon,
who went from being Jim Gordon's partner on

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.480
the police force to the commissioner's second
wife.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.920
Despite Gordon's dedication to keeping the
peace in America's most crime-ridden city,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.950
he and Sarah are happy together even through
the worst of times… until the Clown Prince

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.040
of Crime shows up.

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.980
"...Wait'll they get a load of me.”

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.640
In the finale of the epic, year-long Batman
storyline No Man's Land, in which Gotham City

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.060
was devastated by an earthquake and left to
fend for itself with no support from outside,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.240
the Joker enacted one of his most terrifying
plans.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.000
He kidnapped every baby that had been born
in Gotham during the year that the city was

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.240
isolated off the grid, holding them captive
in the basement of the Gotham Police Department.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.360
Sarah was the first to arrive on the scene,
but she stumbled straight into the madman's

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:16.860
trap.

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:21.480
The Joker tosses a baby at Sarah, and as she
tries to catch the child, he shoots her in

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:21.980
the head.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:26.670
With his work done, the Joker dropped his
weapon, walked outside and immediately surrendered

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:31.090
to the police, defying Jim Gordon to ditch
his "by the book" moral code and shoot him

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.740
and even Batman told Gordon that he wouldn't
stop him if he wanted to take the shot.

00:02:35.069 --> 00:02:39.340
Instead, the Commissioner settled for unloading
his handgun into the Joker's kneecap instead,

00:02:39.341 --> 00:02:43.420
prompting the villain to break out into laughter
at the fact that he might never walk again…

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.240
just like Barbara.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:48.780
Once Dick Grayson grew up and graduated from
the role of Robin into being a hero on his

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:53.060
own as Nightwing, the job of Batman's sidekick
was taken over by Jason Todd.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.840
Unlike Grayson, however, Jason was portrayed
as an edgier character than his predecessor,

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.260
whose rough upbringing in an orphanage had
left him prone to crossing lines that Batman

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.040
never would.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.720
That came to a head in A Death in the Family,
a storyline where Jason ditched the Dark Knight

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.780
and went looking for his long-lost mother.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:12.920
Unfortunately for Jason, he found the Joker,
who delighted in beating the Boy Wonder's

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.220
head in with a crowbar and then blowing up
the body for good measure.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.460
It was the most brutal thing he'd ever done
in comics up to that point, and the loss of

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.740
Robin haunted Batman for years to come.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.600
You can't blame this one entirely on the Joker,
though.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:29.739
Death in the Family had a gimmick, allowing
fans to call in and vote on whether Jason

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.660
would live or die.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:38.190
When the votes were tallied, it came out to
5,271 voting for Robin to live… and 5,343

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.060
calling for his death.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:44.480
With a margin of just 72 votes, Jason was
toast, and the Joker racked up his most famous

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:44.980
kill.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.580
Everyone remembers A Death in the Family for
the scene when the Joker beats Robin to death

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.260
with a crowbar, and for good reason.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:55.420
Still, it's kind of weird that nobody really
talks about how the first part of that story

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.400
is all about the Clown Prince of Crime selling
nuclear weapons to terrorists because his

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.900
previous heists hadn't gone according to plan.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:04.400
"Do I really look like a guy with a plan?"

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:09.180
Obviously, this had less of an impact on the
comics as the whole "killing Batman's sidekick"

00:04:09.190 --> 00:04:13.440
thing, but come on, We all have to agree that
arms deals with terrorists are pretty bad

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.380
in general, right?

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:18.320
Even stranger, it only happened because he
was in desperate need of cash.

00:04:18.329 --> 00:04:22.740
Since he had a spare cruise missile complete
with a nuclear warhead laying around, he decided

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.060
to use it for a quick buck.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.540
Fortunately, the terrorists never got to nuke
Tel Aviv as planned, although Batman didn't

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.120
stop them.

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.340
It turns out that the Joker isn't that great
at nuclear engineering, and after taking the

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:37.420
missile apart to smuggle it into the Middle
East, he didn't put it back together correctly.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:41.370
It ended up exploding in the truck when they
tried to launch it, without detonating the

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.260
nuclear warhead.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.820
While it doesn't get the press of some other
well-known Joker stories, "Soft Targets" is

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.980
one of the absolute best, and features a truly
sinister plot.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.900
It originally ran in 2003 in the pages of
Gotham Central, a book that focused on the

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:59.160
Gotham City Police Department and the way
ordinary people tried to deal with being cops

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:01.780
in a city dominated by superheroes and villains.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:06.860
It showed a grittier side of Gotham without
sacrificing the idea of a world full of super-powers,

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:11.860
and became a fan favorite thanks to its relatable
characters and their very realistic reactions.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:16.200
As you might expect, when the Joker showed
up, those reactions basically amounted to

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.100
sheer terror.

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.340
It started off with a literal bang.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:23.680
A sniper took out Gotham City's mayor with
a headshot, sparking a series of apparently

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:28.210
random killings that terrorized the city in
the weeks before Christmas, even live-streaming

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:30.140
a countdown of his potential targets.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:34.820
Eventually, the police discovered it was the
Batman's arch-nemesis pulling the trigger,

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:38.960
but things took a strange turn — even by
Gotham City standards — when the Joker walked

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:42.860
up to the police station three days before
Christmas and allowed himself to be arrested.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.380
Then came the twist.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:48.360
It turned out that the whole thing — the
assassination of the mayor, the random killings,

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:52.720
the live-streamed sniper attacks — was just
the setup for an even deadlier punchline.

00:05:52.980 --> 00:05:56.440
With the Joker in custody, the people who
had been scared off the streets by the sniper

00:05:56.440 --> 00:06:01.320
attacks scrambled to get their holiday shopping
done, which is exactly what the Joker wanted.

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.040
He'd set bombs in the stockroom of the city's
biggest toy store with plans of explosively

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:08.260
ruining Christmas for Gotham's kids.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:13.740
Fortunately, the GCPD evacuated the civilians,
but when the Joker broke free of the interrogation

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:17.200
room, he managed to rack up a few more gleeful
kills before he was stopped.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:22.820
The animated series Batman Beyond was set
decades in the future, after Bruce Wayne retired

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:27.400
and eventually handed the Batman identity
down to cool young future teen Terry McGinnis.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:31.900
With a few exceptions, Terry's adventures
avoided using established Batman villains,

00:06:31.919 --> 00:06:35.910
instead giving him his own roster of foes
that seemed inspired by Spider-Man's classic

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.560
rogues gallery.

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:41.460
That makes sense, though, since Terry himself
felt like the answer to the question "what

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.580
if Peter Parker became Batman instead?"

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:48.020
When the Joker came back, though, he came
back hard, and brought two incredibly disturbing

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:48.940
reveals with him.

00:06:49.310 --> 00:06:53.020
The first was that before dying, the Joker
had implanted his own consciousness into the

00:06:53.039 --> 00:06:57.720
second Robin, Tim Drake, so that he could
take over his body and re-emerge years later

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.060
to continue terrorizing Gotham after death.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.400
The other, more disturbing, reveal was how
he pulled it off.

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.880
Thirty-five years earlier, he and Harley Quinn
had kidnapped Tim, holding him for weeks before

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:09.100
Batman tracked them down.

00:07:09.509 --> 00:07:13.620
The Joker and Harley spent that time torturing
Robin, breaking him mentally and transforming

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:17.910
him physically into "Joker Junior," complete
with the chalk-white skin and permanently

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:18.780
fixed grin.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.940
"You've lost Batman.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.700
Robin is mine.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:26.900
The last sound you hear will be our laughter."

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.760
When the Joker showed off his handiwork to
Batman and tried to force his new "son" to

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:35.120
kill the hero, Tim managed to break free just
long enough to shoot the Joker instead, killing

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:35.620
him.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:40.680
The image of Tim's maniacal laughter turning
to sobs, with tears streaming down his disfigured

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:45.200
face, is probably the most disturbing thing
to ever hit DC's animated properties.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:50.060
So much so, in fact, that the scene was heavily
edited for its original release, giving the

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:54.360
Joker a very different death scene and eliminating
the more explicit references to torture.

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:59.060
The uncut version has been available since
2003, however, just in case you want to see

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.760
how dark those cartoons can get.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.720
When DC relaunched their line in 2011 as the
"New 52," the first thing the Joker did was

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:10.610
arrange to have his own face cut off by a
villain called the Dollmaker so that he could

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:13.140
leave it hanging in his cell at Arkham when
he escaped.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:17.420
That might be the single weirdest thing he's
ever done, but it wasn't the worst.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:21.380
When he returned a few years later to cut
everyone else's face off, though, that definitely

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.380
made the list.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:27.020
At the climax of the Death Of the Family story
arc not to be confused with Death In the Family

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:30.440
Batman was put through a gauntlet of villains
as he made his way through Arkham.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:35.199
In the end, he was overwhelmed and captured,
waking up at a long dinner table to find the

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.000
Joker waiting for him.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.580
Of course, the Dark Knight isn't the only
guest at this particular party.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:44.050
The Joker had also "invited" Batgirl, along
with the current and former Robins, tied up

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:45.780
with their faces heavily bandaged.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:50.020
In front of each victim, there's a serving
platter covered with a sterling silver dome.

00:08:50.140 --> 00:08:54.731
Then, in a ghoulish twist, out comes Alfred
with a grin stretched from ear to ear, no

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:57.140
doubt caused by the Joker's infamous toxin.

00:08:57.649 --> 00:09:01.399
When Alfred then lifts the domes from each
plate, the Batman Family members finally see

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:05.060
the evening's gruesome meal: their own faces,
looking back at them.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:09.800
Thankfully, after Batman escapes his confinement,
he unwraps the bandages from his family and

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.060
realizes it's all been one sick joke.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:13.540
Everyone's faces are fine.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.240
The Joker just wanted to have a little sadistic
fun.

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:20.960
It does leave us with the question, though:
if those weren't the Batman Family's faces,

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:21.700
whose were they?

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:26.620
While he's usually found in and around Gotham
City, the Joker occasionally shows up in some

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.180
pretty unexpected places.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.639
The nine-part Emperor Joker storyline, for
example, happened in the Superman comics,

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:36.280
and involved one of the most terrifying premises
any comic book reader could imagine.

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:42.079
In that story, Superman's old foe Mister Mxyzptlk,
the magical, fifth-dimensional imp who uses

00:09:42.079 --> 00:09:46.660
his reality warping powers to mess with Superman
every few months, decides to see what would

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:49.320
happen if he handed off those powers to another
trickster.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:52.660
To find out, he gives the Joker just one percent
of his magic.

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:57.680
That would be bad enough, but the Joker manages
to trick Mxyzptlk into giving him the other

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.240
99% to go along with it.

00:09:59.760 --> 00:10:04.160
With these incredible powers, he entertains
himself by remaking the world in his own twisted

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:04.660
image.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:09.120
As you might expect, he spends a lot of time
on Batman, torturing the Dark Knight to death

00:10:09.139 --> 00:10:13.459
every night and then resurrecting him every
morning to do it again, which traumatizes

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:18.040
Batman to the point where Superman erases
his memories to keep him sane His most disturbing

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:18.540
act, though?

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:21.040
Eating the entire population of China.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.040
Yes, really.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:27.600
He eats every single person in China, and
in true Joker style, he uses a pair of chopsticks.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.900
There's a sick sense of humor, and then there's
absolute depravity.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:35.720
If you ever want to see the Joker at his scariest,
do yourself a favor and pick up a copy of

00:10:35.730 --> 00:10:40.939
The Batman Adventures #3 from 1992, because
there's a sequence in that issue that's still

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.640
terrifying all these years later.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:48.060
As he so frequently does, the Joker takes
over Gotham City's airwaves with his own broadcast.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:52.340
His guest is Jim Gordon, kidnapped and tied
up in front of the cameras while the Joker

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:57.239
offers up a monologue that a full 16 years
before The Dark Knight is devoted to the idea

00:10:57.239 --> 00:11:02.249
that law and order are false ideas, and that
the only thing that truly exists is "random

00:11:02.249 --> 00:11:03.249
destructive chaos."

00:11:03.249 --> 00:11:09.280
"Upset the established order and everything
becomes chaos.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.820
I’m an agent of chaos."

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:17.019
To illustrate his point, he punctuates his
speech by picking up a baseball bat and breaking

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:21.000
Gordon's arms while the horrified citizens
of Gotham, and Batman, watch.

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:25.740
It's pretty grim stuff, but here's the best
and worst part: The Batman Adventures was

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:31.110
the tie-in book set in the universe of Batman:
The Animated Series, and as mature and forward-thinking

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:34.000
as that show was, it was still a cartoon for
children.

00:11:34.280 --> 00:11:38.139
This was a comic aimed at younger readers
that featured the Joker announcing that in

00:11:38.139 --> 00:11:41.959
a world that was just, he wouldn't be able
to just pick up a bat and start beating on

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:46.260
a beloved heroic police commissioner, and
then proved himself correct by doing just

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:46.760
that.

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.480
That's a weird thing to learn when you're
still trying to get a handle on subtraction.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:55.660
Since being introduced on Batman: The Animated
Series, Harley Quinn has made the leap to

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:59.279
comics, movies, and more to become one of
DC's most popular characters.

00:11:59.279 --> 00:12:03.040
A big part of that popularity comes down to
the idea that for a villain, she's always

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.660
been incredibly sympathetic.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:09.059
She's a participant in the Joker's madness
and mayhem, but ultimately, he's the one pulling

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:12.580
the strings, manipulating and abusing her
into going along with it.

00:12:12.780 --> 00:12:16.760
Considering all that he's done to her over
the years, it's easy to argue that their entire

00:12:16.769 --> 00:12:21.060
relationship be counted as a whole among the
worst things the Joker has ever done, but

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:25.319
there's a singular example in the pages of
Mad Love, the graphic novel that gave us Harley's

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:25.820
origin.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:29.899
When she takes it upon herself to capture
Batman and "improve" one of his discarded

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.880
deathtrap jokes, the Joker flies into a rage.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:37.040
He backhands her while ranting about how she
doesn't get the joke, then knocks her through

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.800
a window to a five-story fall.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:42.920
She survives, of course, but only through
chance, and only to find herself going back

00:12:42.920 --> 00:12:43.760
to him in the end.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.380
The story was adapted for Batman: The Animated
Series in 1999, but it would be another decade

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:53.400
before readers would get to see Harley breaking
away from the Joker on the page and the screen.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.340
The Joker has been undeniably successful in
the world of thematic villainy, and pretty

00:12:58.350 --> 00:13:02.499
much anything he's done for the past couple
decades has been more like gilding an increasingly

00:13:02.500 --> 00:13:03.420
deadly lily.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:08.049
He's already Batman's arch-nemesis, he's already
the deadliest and most feared criminal in

00:13:08.049 --> 00:13:12.730
DC's considerable roster of bad guys, and
if you think of villainy as being like a sport,

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.220
then there's really nothing else to do.

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:18.649
As a result, you might think that if and when
the Joker finally died, he'd be able to look

00:13:18.649 --> 00:13:22.649
back on his life, tally up the final body
count, and be satisfied that his work was

00:13:22.649 --> 00:13:23.600
finally done.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.740
You would be wrong.

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:28.760
Not only has the Joker managed to ensure that
his reign of terror will continue past his

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:33.740
own death, he's done it in a truly bizarre
way: he booby-trapped his own heart.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:38.560
According to Batman himself, the Joker somehow
laced his cardiovascular system with "a singular

00:13:38.579 --> 00:13:42.779
super-toxin" that will be released at the
moment of his death, turning whoever finally

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:47.540
gives in and kills him his preference, of
course, being Batman into an all-new, all-deadly

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:48.040
Joker.

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:52.239
He even once shot himself to dose Batman,
but fortunately, the Dark Knight managed to

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:55.020
hold off the transformation long enough to
work up a cure.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:59.499
That is some buck wild comic book science
and some pretty advanced biochemistry for

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:04.160
a dude whose major interests include purple
suits and mayhem but it's also a pretty scary

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:04.660
tactic.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:08.860
Not only will he be inflicting his own madness
on someone else, but he'll be ensuring that

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:12.740
it continues indefinitely, ruining countless
more lives at the cost of his own.

00:14:13.140 --> 00:14:16.889
Of course, that only happens if he dies, but
you know things have gotten pretty bad when

00:14:16.889 --> 00:14:20.880
the Joker staying alive to keep on doing what
he does is actually the best option.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:24.959
The Joker's most heinous crime might not be
any of the ones that have happened in the

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.660
comics, or even the movies.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:29.580
Instead, it's part of the backstory of a video
game.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:35.129
In 2013, the Joker showed up in Injustice:
Gods Among Us, a fighting game created by

00:14:35.129 --> 00:14:38.220
NetherRealm Studios, the developers of Mortal
Kombat.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:42.280
Perhaps surprisingly, this video game has
a backstory that was compelling enough to

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:45.900
be the source material for a comic that ran
for a full five years.

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:50.300
To justify the setup of a world where the
superheroes were slugging it out to the death,

00:14:50.309 --> 00:14:54.279
the game took place in an alternate universe
where the Joker pushed Superman well beyond

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:55.180
the breaking point.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:59.880
First, he steals a nuclear submarine, then
he somehow manages to poison the Man of Steel

00:14:59.900 --> 00:15:01.560
with Scarecrow's fear toxin.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:06.320
The poison clouds Superman's mind and makes
him think he's fighting Doomsday, the unstoppable

00:15:06.320 --> 00:15:08.060
monster that once nearly killed him.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:12.999
In reality, he was really unleashing his entire
strength on a target that the Joker chose

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.000
for him instead: Lois Lane.

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.900
Even worse, she was pregnant with Superman's
child.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:23.639
As Lois dies, the launch of a nuclear missile
wipes Metropolis off the map, leaving Superman's

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.620
entire life devastated.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.820
"First Krypton now Metropolis.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:31.560
People you love tend to blow up, don't they?"

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:35.380
As a result, Superman snaps, shoving his fist
through the Joker's chest.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:40.000
Of all the stories where Superman goes bad,
and there are plenty of them, Injustice goes

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.759
to the darkest place that the Man of Steel
had ever been.

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:47.839
It gave us a world where the Joker won, proving
that anybody, even Superman, is capable of

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.140
breaking their own rules if pushed far enough.

